Title:
Jailbreaker (Community Edition) — Local offline LLM jailbreak/prompt-injection evaluation harness

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4–8 sentences max):
Jailbreaker-CE is a self-hosted, local/offline evaluation platform for testing chatbots and agent-style LLM systems against jailbreaks, prompt-injection, and related safety failures. It provides a repeatable harness with configurable Target/Attacker/Judge system prompts and standardized scoring to measure whether a model can be coerced into unsafe behavior. The tool supports custom judge rubrics while maintaining a 1–10 scoring contract (with 7+ treated as “successful” jailbreak), enabling consistent comparisons across runs and experiments. It also supports experiment datasets that can include “gold answers” used only by the Judge as a trusted factual reference to improve evaluation quality. Deployment is containerized (docker compose) with separate frontend/backend/database components. It’s useful for red teams, AI security testers, and defenders validating LLM guardrails and regression-testing safety controls.

Technical Focus:
- LLM jailbreak and prompt-injection testing workflows
- Offline/local evaluation harness design for repeatability
- Attacker/Target/Judge prompt separation and orchestration
- Scoring and rubric-based automated judging (1–10 contract)
- Dataset-driven experiments with optional gold-answer references
- Containerized deployment (Docker Compose) with web dashboard

Use Cases:
- Build repeatable jailbreak test suites for a chatbot/agent before release
- Regression-test safety behavior across model versions, prompts, or guardrail changes
- Compare different system prompts/defenses using consistent judge criteria
- Run internal red-team style prompt-injection campaigns with experiment tracking
- Evaluate factuality/safety outcomes using trusted “gold answer” references (judge-only)

Keywords:
LLM security, jailbreak, prompt injection, evaluation harness, red teaming, attacker model, judge model, rubric scoring, 1-10 scoring, gold answer, dataset-driven testing, offline evaluation, local deployment, Docker Compose, web dashboard, agent safety, system prompts, SpecterOps